WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.876 --> 00:00:03.628
 - I can skate and you
can film, or something.

00:00:03.628 --> 00:00:04.504
- I'll catch it all.

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:05.005
- Let's do it.

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:10.552
 One of the first times I came
to California

00:00:10.552 --> 00:00:12.512
 for a competition,

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:15.682
I was 14 and saw all the
girls that I had looked up to.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:18.643
And I guess that's the
first time that I realized

00:00:18.643 --> 00:00:21.104
this is way cooler
than I even thought.

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.905
 - So you're preparing
for the Olympics.

00:00:30.905 --> 00:00:33.074
You were born in Texas,
grew up in Hawaii,

00:00:33.074 --> 00:00:34.325
currently live in San Diego.

00:00:34.325 --> 00:00:35.744
Now you're going to
be going to Tokyo.

00:00:35.744 --> 00:00:37.287
Did you ever think
that skateboarding

00:00:37.287 --> 00:00:38.538
would take you that far?

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:39.789
- Definitely not.

00:00:39.789 --> 00:00:42.417
It was never a thought really
to make a career out of it when

00:00:42.417 --> 00:00:43.668
I first started skateboarding.

00:00:43.668 --> 00:00:46.254
So for now, to be the
first year in the Olympics,

00:00:46.254 --> 00:00:48.965
it's pretty crazy
how far it's come.

00:00:48.965 --> 00:00:51.384
This is the biggest
competition in the world,

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:53.887
so I want to be as
ready as possible.

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:55.597
I'm very excited
just to go to Japan

00:00:55.597 --> 00:00:58.475
and meet all the other athletes
from so many different sports

00:00:58.475 --> 00:01:01.102
and watch them compete
and learn from them

00:01:01.102 --> 00:01:03.605
and have the whole
Olympic experience.

00:01:09.152 --> 00:01:14.949
OK, so I'm thinking for a
little follow film line—

00:01:14.949 --> 00:01:16.951
- As an NBA player,
I go through tons

00:01:16.951 --> 00:01:19.370
of emotions, tons of
different types of training

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:21.748
from, obviously, regular
season to the postseason.

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:23.792
For you, going
from skating around

00:01:23.792 --> 00:01:26.795
with your friends,
obviously you medal at 17,

00:01:26.795 --> 00:01:28.254
you're an Olympian at 22.

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:30.131
How does your focus,
training, mindset

00:01:30.131 --> 00:01:32.133
shift as you prepare
for Tokyo once you

00:01:32.133 --> 00:01:33.968
get into the actual
skating competition?

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:37.222
- I try to definitely
keep my mindset similar.

00:01:37.222 --> 00:01:39.849
You know, keep it the same, keep
skating, keep doing it

00:01:39.849 --> 00:01:40.642
because I love it.

00:01:40.642 --> 00:01:42.310
That should never
change in my opinion.

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:44.437
- It's a very lonely road
because of the sacrifices

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:47.482
you have to make to get
there, but once you do, it's

00:01:47.482 --> 00:01:48.441
definitely worth it.

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:50.318
- Go that way a tiny bit.

00:01:50.318 --> 00:01:51.111
Now you're good.

00:01:51.111 --> 00:01:51.945
- All right, not moving.

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:52.779
I'm here.

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:54.531
- Skateboarding has
changed my life.

00:01:54.531 --> 00:01:57.200
You go to the skate park and you
don't just learn skateboarding.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.077
You learn a million
life lessons.

00:01:59.077 --> 00:02:02.122
You learn to keep getting
up after you fall, accept

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:02.747
everyone.

00:02:02.747 --> 00:02:04.124
It doesn't matter
if you're good,

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:06.292
you're bad, what race you
are, what gender you are.

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:07.669
We're all just
here skateboarding,

00:02:07.669 --> 00:02:10.213
and we're all having fun, and
everyone encourages everyone.

00:02:10.213 --> 00:02:12.549
It's not like any other sport.

00:02:12.549 --> 00:02:14.175
- Bravo, bravo, bravo.

